impl.entries:
Added (I re-read both files immediately before writing; neither number was taken):
- OQ-163, "The web frame and the demo route of slice S6", in section (g) of OPEN-QUESTIONS.md. It records the [P] engineering choices:
  - route construction and the required clinical flag;
  - the build switch for the demo module;
  - the string-only address format, with ?fixture redirected to ?patient;
  - the address/context sync rules, including hiding the banner while they disagree. This is the stricter reading, and the entry asks the CSO to confirm it;
  - the query cache keyed by patient and pruned after every transition;
  - the store wiring (modal versus hal-capture, random UUID keys from getRandomValues);
  - session user handling, the switch confirmation, the chooser, the frame, the watermark, the CSP with React Aria style hashes and Zod jitless;
  - the extra tests and their timeouts.
- KA-044, the last number of WP-0.7's KA range KA-025…KA-044. It records:
  - production builds have no patient directory, session user or clinical route (fail closed until WP-0.4);
  - a change of user is noticed only on window focus (no BroadcastChannel or shell event);
  - catalogue text that is missing: a chooser label (it reuses "Patients"), no not-found message, and TanStack Router's own English error text on a route error;
  - Chrome lacks Intl data for ckb, so react-intl reports MISSING_DATA;
  - the HAL capture binding is not wired into the web app.

Needed, for the integrator or another slice:
- The KA range is now exhausted. Any further WP-0.7 limitation needs the integrator to extend the range, as was done for OQ-160…169.
- STATUS.md's list of WP-0.7 OQ numbers should add OQ-163, and its next free numbers become OQ-164 and KA range full.

